  <DataPropertyAssertion>
    <DataProperty abbreviatedIRI="kt:description"/>
    <NamedIndividual abbreviatedIRI="kt:issue-cgc-three-nominal-graph"/>
    <Literal>Fixed. When a node lost its completion graph caching, the reactivation followed the nodes that the cached model had merged into it, but not the node that it had been merged into. In cgc-n2-three-nominal-ontology.owl.xml the cached model merged a4 into a2 and a5 into a1; a test that adds a concept to a4 rebuilt a4, while a2 stayed cached with the merge of a4 in its cached state, so the a2 choice was never redone and ({a4} and not A) and ({a4} and {a5}) were answered satisfiable. The same gap made the classification of cgc-n1-exact-cardinality-ontology.owl.xml under reduced saturation miss B below A. CCompletionGraphCacheHandler::getReactivationIndividuals now also reactivates (forced) the cached representative of a node that loses its caching. The classification additionally tested {a4} and {a1}, where the nominal a4 is merged into a test node that already carries the nominal a1; a nominal that is merged into another nominal node did not lose its caching, so mergeIndividualNodeInto now clears the caching of every merged nominal. Guards: kt:cgc-n2-a4-not-a, kt:cgc-n2-a4-a5 and kt:cgc-n2-classification in Tests/cases/cgc-known-n2 (default-config, delayed-caching-reactivation, no-backjumping).</Literal>
  </DataPropertyAssertion>
