  <DataPropertyAssertion>
    <DataProperty abbreviatedIRI="kt:description"/>
    <NamedIndividual abbreviatedIRI="kt:issue-cgc-merge-dependant-reactivation"/>
    <Literal>Fixed. Differential fuzzing (caching on against caching off and HermiT) found four more cases in which a node kept its cached state although a node it shares that state with was rebuilt. (1) Nodes merged into a node through a chain of merges (v into a1, a1 into a0) were not found, only nodes whose final representative is the node (cgc-o1). (2) A node that is taken from the reactivation queue as a forced reactivation did not pass the reactivation on to the nodes merged with it (cgc-o1, cgc-o3); it now calls CCompletionGraphCacheHandler::getMergeDependentReactivationIndividuals, which covers the representative, the merged blockable nodes and the merged nominals but not the connection neighbours (the full caching loss there made the roberts classification about six times slower). (3) CIndividualReactivationProcessingQueue::insertReactivationIndiviudal let a later re-check request turn an earlier forced entry of the same node into a re-check (cgc-o2). (4) The classification message analyser accepted the deterministic concepts of a node into which the tested node was merged by a choice as subsumers (maximum deterministic branch tag 0 still accepts concepts with tag 0); it now accepts none of them in that case (cgc-o4).</Literal>
  </DataPropertyAssertion>
